00³ = 99^99. The unique real cube root is a_100 = 99^33.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_076"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1999_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h200","cnm_076","cnm_143"],"id":"geometric-cubes","label":"Track the cubes of the terms","methodDirectNodeIds":{"geometric-cubes":["cnm_h208"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h208","cnm_h200","cnm_076","cnm_143"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:10a03d3015c4f96d19d5655e"],"answerCheck":{"adjudication":"Native reconciliation under the recorded task assumptions; no blind-review claim.","derivedAnswer":"A, -2","reason":"The inverse composition f(f^-1(x))=x gives ab=1 and a^2+b=0. Hence a!=0, b=-a^2 and a^3=-1. Real solutions give a=b=-1 and a+b=-2. Both affine maps are then -x-1 with the required inverse property.","recordedAnswer":"A","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_076"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2004_AMC_12B_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"compose-the-affine-maps","label":"Use the inverse composition identity","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compose-the-affine-maps":["math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_145","cnm_034","cnm_076"]},"nodeIds":["math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_145","cnm_034","cnm_076"]},{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"solve-for-the-inverse","label":"Find the affine inverse algebraically and solve the parameter condition","methodDirectNodeIds":{"solve-for-the-inverse":["cnm_040","cnm_042","cnm_076"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_040","cnm_042","cnm_076"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h027","cnm_145","cnm_076"],"id":"compose-inverse-functions","label":"Compose the function with its inverse","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compose-inverse-functions":["math:inverse-functions","math:function-composition-iteration"]},"nodeIds":["math:inverse-functions","math:function-compos