"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:10a03d3015c4f96d19d5655e"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 32 cm","reason":"Let the dimensions be u, v, w in geometric progression. Then uw = v² and uvw = v³ = 8, so v = 2. Also uv + uw + vw = v(u + v + w) = 16, giving u + v + w = 8. All edges total 4·8 = 32 cm.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_076"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1985_AMC_12_Q25","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p160","cnm_076"],"id":"use-middle-dimension","label":"Use the middle dimension","methodDirectNodeIds":{"use-middle-dimension":["cnm_h209","cnm_p161","cnm_p163"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h209","cnm_p161","cnm_p163","cnm_p160","cnm_076"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:10a03d3015c4f96d19d5655e"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, square root of (6 times cube root of 5)","reason":"The sixth powers of A through E are respectively 30, 1080, 750, 150, and 180. Since all original expressions are positive, B is largest.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_076"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1990_AMC_12_Q05","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_020","cnm_074","cnm_076"],"id":"compare-sixth-powers","label":"Remove the roots with sixth powers","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compare-sixth-powers":["cnm_h039","cnm_143"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h039","cnm_143","cnm_020","cnm_074","cnm_076"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:10a03d3015c4f96d19d5655e"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D (72)","reason":"The edge lengths are 1, 2, and 3, so the separate surface areas total 6(1+4+9)=84. Pairwise contact areas are at most 4, 1, and 1. All three bounds are attained by placing the two smaller cubes side by side on a face of the largest, touching each other. The exposed area is 84-2(4+1+1)=72.","status":"matches"},"assess